OL,3,GNEWSAOutfit planning, royalty and
OL,4,A45,000 glasses of prosecco - Doncaster
OL,5,Aprepares for race week
OL,6,
OL,7,FIn Doncaster, they say that autumn
OL,8,Fblows in on the tail of the last horse
OL,9,Fhome in the St Leger.
OL,11,FThe old phrase was as true in 1776 as
OL,12,Fit is today, when September's meeting
OL,13,Fat the city's racecourse is still the
OL,14,Fhighlight of the summer social season.
OL,16,FWhen the St Leger Stakes was first run
OL,17,F250 years ago, racing was still the
OL,18,Fsport of the aristocracy, but over the
OL,19,Fnext two centuries Doncaster's growth
OL,20,Fas a railway town meant that race week
OL,21,Fbegan to appeal to the masses.
OL,23,APub: 10-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
